        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Halo-2-CE.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Halo has a proud history of smuggling secret endings into its campaigns. In the very first 2001 game, there is a hidden (non-canon) ending featuring Sgt. Avery Johnson fighting and hugging an Elite. In <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/halo-2\">Halo 2</a>, there's a mid-credits scene that teases the beginning of <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/halo-3\">Halo 3</a>. In Halo 3, we get a full scene of Chief drifting, alone, in the cold, indifferent vacuum of space. ODST gives us a glimpse of the Engineers' secret. And in Reach, my personal favourite, we get that phenomenal 'Lone Wolf' ending that still sends shivers down my spine to think about today.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/halo-2-remake-tease-legendary-ending-campaign-evolved\">Read more</a></p>",
