        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/custom-image-sega-ceo.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Sega is the latest publisher to make its views about physical media clear, in the wake of Sony's controversial decision to <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/sony-ending-playstation-discs-physical-media-january-2028\">kill off the manufacture and sale of discs by 2028</a>. The president of the Japanese publisher, Shuji Utsumi, noted that he believes physical media is still important, though digital distribution is \"crucial\", mostly thanks to the \"steadily increasing\" number of people playing on PC.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-physical-media-sega-ceo\">Read more</a></p>",
