        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Niikawa-discs.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Since 1st July, when Sony <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/sony-ending-playstation-discs-physical-media-january-2028\">announced its intent to move away from the production and sale of physical media</a>, we've seen plenty of backlash from both consumers and those working within the video game industry. There's plenty of evidence of this, but the most vocal and visceral has come <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/marvels-wolverine-story-trailer-sony-disc-outrage\">from comments on pretty much anything Sony has posted</a> online in the days since the announcement.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-physical-media-hardware-disgaea-creator\">Read more</a></p>",
